Pushback and caveats
The sunspot chart will look almost flat, and that is correct for this model. Within P.368 and P.372, the solar cycle only changes galactic-noise screening. In reality the solar-cycle effects on HFSWR come from ionospheric self-clutter and sky-wave interference, and the ITU framework does not model those. Medium confidence that this matters operationally.
A constant 1 m² radar cross-section understates real air targets at HF, where resonance makes the cross-section rise steeply with frequency.
Sea-roughness (Barrick) losses are not included. They will reduce ranges further above about 15 MHz in rough seas.
