One model change you should know about

To make the speed chart meaningful I steepened the far tail of the second-order clutter spectrum. It now falls as Δf⁻⁵, matching the tail of the wave spectrum, instead of Δf⁻⁴. This raised some ranges at 50 m/s, for example from about 13 km to 30 km at 5 MHz around noon. It is the right physics in direction, but the second-order model is still parametric, so treat its absolute levels with medium-low confidence.

